  "description": "Adiantum pedatum, commonly known as Northern Maidenhair Fern or American Maidenhair Fern, is a deciduous fern native to moist forests of North America (eastern US and Canada). It belongs to the Pteridaceae family and features distinctive fronds with a horizontal, fan-shaped blade on a dark, wiry stipe; leaflets (pinnae) are arranged in a horseshoe or finger-like pattern. Foliage is bright green in spring and summer, turning yellow in autumn. It grows 30-60 cm tall with a similar spread and prefers shade to part shade and consistently moist, humus-rich soil. Non-toxic. Suitable for shaded terrariums, paludariums, and outdoor shade gardens in temperate regions.",
